      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You must immediately pivot your messaging to acknowledge the moral weight of colonial history while clarifying that returning artifacts is a complex legal and logistical process, not a simple yes-or-no decision. Ignoring the activists' concerns will only deepen public anger, so you need to frame the museum's role as one of stewardship and education rather than just legal ownership. The best strategy is to launch a transparent dialogue about repatriation timelines and community partnerships, showing that you are actively working to address the ethical critique even if you cannot return every item right now.",
      "source": "target",
