      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to be concerned; simply repeating legal jargon while ignoring the moral critique will make you look like you are protecting your own interests at the expense of justice. To defend your legal rights without appearing self-serving, you must explicitly acknowledge that the current legal framework is outdated and that the museum is actively working to dismantle the very colonial structures that created the \"ownership\" claim in the first place. Your messaging must shift from defending the *right* to hold the items to defending the *responsibility* to eventually return them, framing the legal defense as a temporary bridge to a more ethical future rather than a permanent shield.",
